License structure
-----------------

* The upstream IOPaint code (the `iopaint/` package, `web_app/`, `setup.py`,
  and other base files) remains licensed under Apache-2.0. Some of these files
  have been modified for the darktable integration; per Apache-2.0 section 4,
  such modifications are noted here and recorded in the project's git history.
  The modified upstream files are:
    - iopaint/api.py        — adds the `/api/v1/connected_clients`, `/api/v1/presets`
                              (GET/POST), `/api/v1/server_log`, `/api/v1/models`,
                              `/api/v1/download_model` and `/api/v1/cancel`
                              endpoints (the last interrupts a running diffusion
                              inference)
    - iopaint/cli.py        — adds the `--preset-file` and `--log-file` options to
                              `iopaint start`
    - iopaint/schema.py     — adds `preset_file` and `log_file` to `ApiConfig`
    - iopaint/const.py      — adds the `--preset-file` / `--log-file` help text
    - iopaint/helper.py     — replaces the removed stdlib `imghdr` with Pillow
    - iopaint/download.py    — detects inpaint diffusers models by UNet
                              in_channels (fixes model-type misclassification);
                              retries downloads on transient Hub-connection errors
    - iopaint/model_manager.py — always runs switch_controlnet_method /
                              switch_brushnet_method so disabling ControlNet or
                              BrushNet takes effect (was skipped when toggled off)
    - requirements.txt      — relaxes pinned dependencies for newer Python
    - web_app/ (frontend)   — adds the Presets dropdown, fixes the HD
                              crop-strategy request fields, removes the "Buy me a
                              coffee" link, replaces the linear undo stack with a
                              toggleable patch/layer history opened from a floating
                              "Edit history" button (History panel), consolidates
                              the mutually-exclusive cropper / extender / patch-fill
                              workflows into a tab strip in the right panel, adds
                              the "Patch fill" auto-tiling workflow (sliding-window
                              inpainting of a whole masked area with a live tile
                              preview), auto-enables and sizes the cropper for
                              oversized diffusion images, and lets the History panel
                              inspect a patch's settings, reuse its mask, and reapply
                              its settings, adds stop buttons to the progress
                              bars (per-inference and patch-fill) that cancel
                              processing, and persists the in-progress edit
                              session (source image + history) to IndexedDB so a
                              reload after a transient failure restores the work

